in...HEAD -- cadence","description":"Show diff for cadence vs origin/main"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01CVYofdWjG475fgC5MoHa6K","tool_input":{"command":"git -C /home/drspeedracer/Workspace/spotify-recsys-ecosystem-spot-7lj diff origin/main...HEAD -- cadence","description":"Show diff of cadence against origin/main"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uu5zASZ1EGn5tBNvoSLPup","tool_input":{"command":"git -C /home/drspeedracer/Workspace/spotify-recsys-ecosystem-spot-7lj diff origin/main...HEAD -- cadence","description":"Show diff against origin/main for cadence"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_014Ttk8DgvRADnSpJRz2CFhe","tool_input":{"command":"gh pr list --state open --json number,title,headRefName,baseRefName","description":"List open PRs to find the parent"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_019LewjyUUogrC5FAbMDrNr3","tool_input":{"command":"gh pr list --state open","description":"List open pull requests"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01QuMAMVjEL83N83Cb1asW4J","tool_input":{"command":"git fetch origin --quiet; git merge-base --is-ancestor fca524a origin/fleet/builder-permissions && echo IN_BUILDER_PERMS || echo NOT_IN_BUILDER_PERMS; git merge-base --is-ancestor fca524a origin/main && echo IN_MAIN || echo NOT_IN_MAIN","description":"Check where parent commits landed"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01PUnHfD8cHLYGqyiuRF4KPQ","tool_input":{"command":"git fetch origin","description":"Fetch latest refs from origin"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01PcKP3eGPGqBR1Trt6aUJeF","tool_input":{"command":"gh pr create --base fleet/builder-permissions --head bead/spot-7lj --title \"spot-7lj: persist per-challenge metric vectors and report paired deltas\" --body \"## What the bead asked for\n\n\\`run_eval.py\\` gives every arm the identical challenge list in identical order, and \\`MetricAccumulator.values\\` already holds the per-challenge vector — but \\`summary()\\` collapsed it to mean+SE and threw the pairing away. Measured cross-arm correlation is rho 0.9922–0.9995, so pairing buys 128–2171x variance reduction for zero extra compute (bead spot-7lj, P0).\n\n## What this does\n\n- \\`MetricAccumulator.paired_deltas(reference)\\`: per-challenge differencing against an arm run over the same challenges; emits \\`{metric}_delta\\`, \\`{metric}_delta_se\\`, \\`{metric}_n_changed\\`. Sign is arm minus reference. Misaligned vectors raise instead of pairing garbage.\n- Every non-reference arm in each report cell (ablations, reranked, and the three baselines — all score the same list) now carries those fields, paired against \\`full_fusion\\`. \\`meta.paired_reference\\` records the convention.\n- The per-challenge vectors are persisted to \\`eval_report_vectors.json\\` next to the report (whitelisted in .gitignore), and \\`verify_vectors()\\` re-derives every mean, SE, and delta from the sidecar to 1e-9 **before** either file is written, so report and sidecar cannot drift apart. It also refuses a sidecar that lost a vector, an arm, or its meta, and NaN fails the check instead of slipping through.\n\n## How the acceptance criteria are met\n\n- *Means reproduce exactly*: the scoring loop is untouched — arms hand back the accumulator they always had, and \\`summary()\\`'s arithmetic is unchanged. The printed progress lines are also byte-identical.\n- *Sidecar re-derives every mean to 1e-9*: \\`verify_vectors()\\` runs inside \\`run()\\` on every eval, and \\`test_published_report_agrees_with_its_sidecar_to_1e9\\` checks the committed artifacts on disk (it skips until a sidecar exists, like the other artifact-dependent tests).\n- *Paired 2SE below unpaired*: the same on-disk test asserts \\`2*delta_se < 2*sqrt(se_a^2+se_b^2)\\` for every arm and cell, which for \\`no_cooccurrence\\` r_precision at k=5 is the published 0.0204 band.\n\n## Deliberately left out\n\n- **The regenerated \\`eval_report.json\\` + sidecar.** This worktree has no \\`data/processed\\` or model artifacts, so I could not run \\`cadence evaluate --limit 400\\`. The committed report is unchanged; whoever holds the data runs \\`make -C cadence eval\\` once, and the disk test stops skipping and enforces the acceptance numbers. That run is the remaining acceptance step.\n- No doc updates (\\`docs/EVALUATION.md\\`) — the in-flight spot-ktp bead is rewriting how published numbers cite their floors; touching it here would collide.\n\nPanel review ran (3 lenses): 9 findings, 5 accepted and fixed in the third commit, 3 rejected, 1 out-of-scope (parent branch's code); all in \\`.flywheel/review.jsonl\\`.\n\nStacks on the spot-2ig work already merged to \\`fleet/builder-permissions\\`, hence the base branch.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\"","description":"Open PR for bead spot-7lj"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":3,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":3,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":3,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"general-purpose":3}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":109,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Done. Report:\n\n**Bead taken:** spot-7lj (P0) — persist per-challenge metric vectors and report paired deltas.\n\n**What I did:** Added `MetricAccumulator.paired_deltas()` (per-challenge differencing vs a reference arm → `{metric}_delta` / `_delta_se` / `_n_changed`, raising on misaligned vectors), wired every non-reference arm in each eval cell to carry those fields against `full_fusion`, and persisted the per-challenge vectors to an `eval_report_vectors.json` sidecar. `verify_vectors()` re-derives every mean, SE, and delta from the sidecar to 1e-9 before either file is written, and an on-disk test enforces both the re-derivation and paired-band < unpaired-band against the committed artifacts. The scoring loop is untouched, so existing means reproduce exactly.\n\n**Gate:** green — 130 tests pass, ruff check + format clean, mypy clean. Panel review (3 lenses) found 9 issues: 5 accepted and fixed (one-directional verification, unignored sidecar, KeyError vs ValueError, NaN slipping through tolerance, no external verifier caller), 3 rejected with reasons, 1 out-of-scope; all recorded in `.flywheel/review.jsonl`.\n\n**PR:** [#9](https://github.com/jamesponwith/spotify-recsys-ecosystem/pull/9), based on `fleet/builder-permissions` since it stacks on the merged spot-2ig work. Bead left open with `w:2`, PR noted, audit log updated.\n\n**Deliberately left out / caveat:** this worktree has no `data/processed` or model artifacts, so I could not execute `cadence evaluate --limit 400`. The remaining acceptance step is one `make -C cadence eval` run on the machine holding the data — the committed report is unchanged until then, and the disk test skips until the sidecar exists. This is noted on the bead and in the PR. Worktree left in place for the orchestrator (my session runs inside it); reservations released; nothing merged.","ttft_ms":2879,"type":"result","duration_ms":989093,"uuid":"13f87b19-d2ef-47fd-aa79-bb846a826293","ttft_stream_ms":1758,"time_to_request_ms":143,"queued_turn_count":0}
